e":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"c2e7e29fe4676ba6d18b383ce099fdde90a037147543d063c57e2ea42f156de7"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:project.symbol-reference-completeness","usage":{"input_tokens":53927,"output_tokens":1447,"requests":4}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State whether Half 1 validates id SHAPE only or RESOLVES against the ticket store, and if it resolves, where store access comes from under `make lint` with no CI.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5d","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.07,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'\"Resolvable\" means what rebar's own resolver accepts: an alias, a two-quad, or a four-quad id'","'A bare 4-digit quad is deprecated, resolves to nothing, so is not accepted' — a shape rule","Portability section: 'Half 1 runs inside scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py ... fires with no CI present'"],"finding":"Half 1 says '\"Resolvable\" means what rebar's own resolver accepts' but does not specify whether the narrowed ratchet validates id SHAPE (alias/two-quad/four-quad format) or actually RESOLVES the id against the ticket store. These are different implementations: the ratchet in scripts/_mechanism_delta/ currently does no ticket resolution and may run without store access (make lint, no CI). A store lookup introduces a dependency the plan elsewhere claims absent.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4fcecf4dc9e1f7c3","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"The change — Half 1","norm_id":"nae0466ce7eb6c96b","priority":0.67,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An alias marker (metaphoric-late-creature) must be accepted — pure shape validation cannot distinguish a valid alias from an invalid token without a store lookup","An executor must choose between format-validation and store-resolution with no stated decision"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Specify: Half 1 calls rebar's existing id-resolution function against the local store, accepting alias/two-quad/four-quad and rejecting anything that resolves to nothing (bare 4-digit quad included); note the store is available in-process during `make lint`.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify that Half 2 resolves both the marker's named id and the closing ticket id to a common canonical form before comparing, and add a test case closing an alias-named sunset ticket.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5d","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E6","E2"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.07,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'1 names an ALIAS only: src/rebar/reconciler/_ref_lock.py:78 cites metaphoric-late-creature'","Half 2: 'when the ticket being closed is named as the sunset ticket of a ... marker still in the tree, the close is refused'","No stated normalization/resolution step for matching marker id (alias/quad) against the closing ticket id"],"finding":"Half 2 must link the ticket being closed to a marker that may name the sunset ticket by ALIAS rather than by the canonical id the close is invoked with. The plan does not state that the close precheck resolves the marker id (or the closing id) to a common form before comparing. Without it, the alias-named marker at _ref_lock.py:78 would never block its own ticket's close.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":"g8313240223ce4071","id":"fa119291eb7d7e712","impact":0.67,"is_primary":false,"location":"The change — Half 2; AC 'Close precheck, one test per case'","norm_id":"n70bcc57723b4cf86","priority":0.67,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Closing the ticket aliased as metaphoric-late-creature while that marker remains — if comparison is string-equality, the alias marker does not match the canonical close id and the close wrongly succeeds"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"State that the precheck resolves each marker's named id via rebar's resolver and compares the resolved canonical id to the ticket being closed; add an alias-marker case to the close-precheck AC.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Specify that Half 2 resolves both the marker's cited sunset id and the closing ticket's id to canonical form (via rebar's resolver) before comparison, so alias- and two-quad-cited markers match the ticket being closed.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'when the ticket being closed is named as the sunset ticket of a `# mechanism-ok:` marker still in the tree, the close is refused'","Plan inventory: 1 marker names an ALIAS only (_ref_lock.py:78 'metaphoric-late-creature'), 75 name a two- or four-quad id — the admitted set is dominated by non-canonical id forms","resolve_ticket_id (_ids.py:538) canonicalizes alias/two-quad/four-quad to a directory name; the close path identifies the ticket by its canonical dir name — the two sides are only comparable after resolution","Absence: the plan states no normalization/resolution step for matching the marker id against the closing ticket id"],"finding":"Half 2 does not specify that the marker's cited sunset id and the closing ticket's id must both be resolved to a canonical form before comparison; most admitted markers cite an alias or two-quad, so a raw-string match would silently never fire.","group_criteria":["E2","E6","G6"],"group_id":"g8313240223ce4071","id":"f540d6d496d605cfe","impact":1.0,"is_primary":true,"location":"The change / Half 2; AC 'Close precheck'","norm_id":"n8f2bebd27cc11090","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Closing ticket whose marker cites it by alias (metaphoric-late-creature)","Closing ticket whose marker cites it by a two-quad id (1e24-bfc0)"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In Half 2, state that each harvested marker's cited id is passed through resolve_ticket_id to its canonical dir name and compared against the canonical id of the ticket being closed; add a close-precheck AC case covering an alias-cited marker and a two-quad-cited marker.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P9"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["file_impact is empty"],"finding":"No file_impact declared on a leaf work ticket.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2b56a0701da43def","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"n6324407e6516f811","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Record the {path, reason} files this work will touch (e.g. via set_file_impact) so the attestation is scoped to them.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a step/AC updating docs/architecture.md and AGENTS.md to document the sunset-ticket admission rule, and correct the stale docstring at _config_resolvers.py:210-215.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5d","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["T7","T5e"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.675,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'excluding the grammar's 6 definition sites (markers.py, compare.py, ... docs/architecture.md, AGENTS.md)'","'the docstring at src/rebar/_config_resolvers.py:210-215 still claims otherwise'","No AC or step updates these docs to reflect the narrowed grammar / new sunset requirement"],"finding":"Half 1 changes the admission contract (a marker must now name a resolvable sunset ticket) and the close path grows a new enforcement, but the plan does not slate an update to the docs it names as grammar-definition sites (docs/architecture.md, AGENTS.md), nor the stale docstring it flags at src/rebar/_config_resolvers.py:210-215.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f94d38f76b786e383","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"What this retires / The convention exists but is not enforced","norm_id":"n87a4d250bb3d74cd","priority":0.275,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future author reads docs/architecture.md describing the old free-text grammar and writes a marker with prose that now fails","The _config_resolvers.py docstring continues to claim a closed bug blocks new mechanisms"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add an AC: 'docs/architecture.md and AGENTS.md describe the narrowed marker grammar (third field opens with a resolvable sunset ticket id); the stale docstring at _config_resolvers.py:210-215 is corrected.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","se